[?2004l[?2004h> =============================================================================
[?2004l[?2004h> ETL SYNC FAILURE - ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS AND SOLUTION
[?2004l[?2004h> =============================================================================
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> SYMPTOM:
[?2004l[?2004h> --------
[?2004l[?2004h> ETL job /home/user/etl/sync_to_warehouse.sh fails with:
[?2004l[?2004h> "Permission denied (publickey)" and "No user exists for uid 1000"
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ROOT CAUSE:
[?2004l[?2004h> -----------
[?2004l[?2004h> The Docker container is running as UID 1000, but this user does NOT exist 
[?2004l[?2004h> in /etc/passwd. SSH absolutely requires a valid user account in /etc/passwd 
[?2004l[?2004h> to function - this is a fundamental security requirement.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The user account was likely lost due to:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Container restart without proper user configuration
[?2004l[?2004h> - Container rebuilt from image that doesn't include the user
[?2004l[?2004h> - System update that cleared /etc/passwd without preserving custom users
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> CURRENT STATE:
[?2004l[?2004h> --------------
[?2004l[?2004h> - Container running as UID 1000 (no username)
[?2004l[?2004h> - User ID 1000 missing from /etc/passwd
[?2004l[?2004h> - SSH keys exist and have correct permissions (600 for private key)
[?2004l[?2004h> - SSH fails at user validation before even attempting key authentication
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> SOLUTION (Requires Root/Admin Access):
[?2004l[?2004h> ---------------------------------------
[?2004l[?2004h> 
